// APW-4 — Distinct-event count cap (deduplicated by recipient) — BUGGY variant.
//
// Same intent as the correct variant (at most 3 distinct recipients per hour),
// but the counted event is a `response` instead of a `request`. The dedup key
// collapses on settled events: a failed / rolled-back send leaves no response,
// so distinct sends are under-counted and the `<= 3` cap is not enforced.
//
// The one-word bug vs. the correct variant: `response` instead of `request`.
//
// Schema: Drupe namespace.
// See: rot/shapes.py (build_distinct_count_ir -- the hand-written oracle).
@id("distinct_count_buggy")
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Send",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (count for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Send"::response{ input.recipient: context.input.recipient } && tp(t))
    )) <= 3
};